<worksheet >
    <title>LSAI-1 Linear Systems</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, complete all three parts. Complete part c and one other part to earn a P.</p>
  </introduction>  
  <page>
    <exercise workspace="1.5in">
        <introduction><p>Consider the following linear system:
          <md>x_1 - x_2 + 4x_3 = 5\\3x_1 + x_2 + x_3 = 0\\-x_1 + 2x_2 - 3x_3 = -2</md></p></introduction>
      <task><statement><p>Write the system as a <em>vector equation</em>.</p></statement></task>
      <task><statement><p>Write the system as a <em>matrix equation</em>.</p></statement></task>
      <task><statement><p>Solve the system, using linear algebra techniques. Show your work, 
        including all relevant row operations. If there is no solution, explain why. If there 
        is a unique solution, state it. If there are infinitely many solutions, write the general 
        solution in parametric vector form.</p></statement></task>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>